{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1085411-eldagusto-s-wyld-west-game","id":1085411,"title":"Eldagusto's Wyld West game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-29T03:17:06-07:00","id":1085411,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon10.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Eldagusto's Wyld West game","content":"So my side game in Between Exalted turns out is going to be Werewolf the Wyld West! I love Werewolf, I truly do! So my players never experienced CWOD games so it will be a treat. One player is making a British Homid Fianna Galliard, and she wants to be my first player to ever choose Intelligence 1! I am thrilled about this, no one ever does that in games! Grog in Critical Role is the only player I seen do this! One player is making a Lupus, Theurge, Uktena. <br /> <br /> The last is making a Metis Uktena, probably Ragabash. Now this kooky customer had some crazy notions... his first thought was he wanted to be a Katana Wielding Fireball throwing Werewolf, yeah seriously in a wild west game... such a Treat! They do exist! But he wanted to make a Freak Assassin, so Metis Ragabash seemed the best fit. Now he also had some madness when he insisted Wendigo was a word made up by Theodore Roosevelt in a horror book he wrote... which I'm pretty sure isn't a thing. I think he is confusing it for Algernon Blackwood's Wendigo story, and I tried assuaging him it was a northern tribal story, Algonquian.<br /> <br /> But anyhooooo I'm still deciding on specifics. I think I will want to probably want to do a game in California, but maybe Texas or Arizona. And the time period I am trying to figure when, but I am thinking sometime around 1873-1883.<br /> <br /> One more player may play, but since this is the game we will play when someone is missing in our Exalted game during cliff hangers, this is the most likely to not be there player. I don't know what he will be, but maybe it won't be a pack member, otherwise they would be NPC or missing much of the time. Hell maybe he could be a Kinfolk Sorcerer or something, or a Silent Strider or Ronin.<br /> <br /> But I am thinking maybe I will give the group some NPC Packmates, this would be a great idea for the whole emotion from them dying later! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Werewolf is much simpler then Exalted so I'm not worried about adding NPCs to help the group. How often do you'all make NPC packmates? One Player has a Mentor, but a high level one so probably shouldn't be a pack member as it would be the likely leader unless it chose not to be.<br /> <br /> But with two Uktena members we are considering the Lupus and Metis being Brothers. Since neither are Homid I am trying to think about what tribal kinfolk to tie them to, so they would have a non English Language. Its a hard choice, maybe a Tribe found in the Area like Shoshoni or Mojave. Native American Languages are not my specialty so I need to research how their languages are grouped. Any advice on this?<br /> <br /> I'm permitting Sorcery so I am pretty sure one or both the Uktena are going to invest in it. I will use a combination of Sorcerer Revised, and the Foci rules in M20.<br /> <br /> Since they are a small group we are considering why they are grouped together, we may just have it be an Uktena dominated pack with the Fianna as a tag along, maybe she will try to be one of the ones trying to either make amends or share wisdom. I may add like two NPCs, if I do maybe one or both will be Uktena, or maybe one will be a Fianna relative, and a Bonegnawer.<br /> <br /> Honestly I love the Enlightened Society of the Weeping Moon, more even then Pentex. I plan to give them access to more Sorcery then the two Saturnal Paths. And maybe a Nephandi joining.<br /> <br /> So thoughts, when learning Sorcery from a Mage, would it be Mages teaching essentially static versions of the magic they wield, so if they are a Force mage they may know a Path of Flames to teach? I permit Mages to also learn Sorcery in my games, so there is also the the plain option of mages only being able to teach paths they know, but I like the idea of Mages being trailblazers and teaching Paths even if they don't know them.<br /> <br /> I have plans for several other antagonists.<br /> <br /> -Leeches. Vampires trying to claim the west. Like Warlocks starting up chantries, and a Coven of Baali who are creating something similar to Gargoyles, a Bloodline I call the Brood of Belial, or Slaves. Basically using a right similar to At My Command It Breathes, the Baali stitch together Cainites, and possibly animal parts to make animalistic Slaves resembling things like the Baphomet.<br /> <br /> -A Taftani Mage making a hidden Seraglio in the desert, claiming servants brought from the old country as well as talented locals, and earning the attention of the pack by kidnapping a young Kinfolk of the Uktena who just awakened and he plans to make his new apprentice. He is investigating the West because of rumors of the Storm Umbra, and its effects on nullifying Paradox, as well as tracking down a Lost Pot o'Djinn.<br /> <br /> -The Grandest Adventure Lodge, a secret society of hunters who cannibalize humans and hunt Supernaturals as a source of Strength, think a mix of the Movie Ravenous, and the Episode Super Adventure Club from Southpark but tied to the Eater of Souls Rather then the Defiler Wyrm.<br /> <br /> We are still deciding things but I would love suggestions and discussion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I figure I will do a Group Right of Passage as the First Session after the Prelude, or actually as the end of the Prelude.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh some questions. I am thinking about Specialties and Craft. And deciding if I want to do the system where you just take different specialties to represent different Crafts/Science training, or just have them buy each as a separate skill. I mean CWOD compared to Exalted you have abilities up the Wazoo.<br /> <br /> I am using Integrity as a Talent, and using Guile and Resolve like in Exalted, and Intimacies. I like the system and want to test out using that. Without Socialize I am having Guile use Subterfuge, but potentially other abilities in a situational basis, like Etiquette at a ball. I also plan to use Static DVs for evasion and Parry. But I am thinking I may use Soak like 2nd ed Exalted were it just removes dice from the damage roll, or I may just have them roll it. What are thoughts on this? Anyone try these out?<br /> <br /> Willpower will only be a trait for how much temp willpower you have, for Willpower rolls I will use Integrity and Wits, vampires use this for Thaumaturgy as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh I plan to also try the old, Hidden Nuwisha Packmate Trick hehe...<br /> <br /> <br /> Another issue is Merits... Normally I mostly ignored Merits, as they were optional, but when you make Language a Merit they are no longer really optional. So I guess without a good reason no one will probably get them, and I don't mind give them out though if they want em.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thoughts and Advice? The Crafting and Soak rules in particular I would love to hear about, as well as suggestions for Aboriginal tribes for players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-01T07:32:22-07:00","id":1086190,"title":"","content":"Oh another question, what do you think the comparative populations of the Wild West's shifter numbers compared to modern times? Were there more of them? Or do we have more werewolves in Modern Times because the World has so much more humans, So the Wild West just has a significantly greater ratio of Garou to Humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T01:04:12-07:00","id":1088653,"title":"","content":"Okay with Changeling 20 finally out, I return to an old curious passion of mine, what if I reveal over the course of the Story that the Pack is actually composed of Kinain! So the Fianna are tied to the Kithain, and the Uktena tied to the Nunnehi, and maybe the Metis tied to Both, with the Nuwisha as the only member not actually a Kinain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T01:15:10-07:00","id":1088657,"title":"","content":"If a St did that in a game I was playing in I would probably stop attending their game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 05-06-2017, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T02:07:51-07:00","id":1088665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1085411-eldagusto-s-wyld-west-game?p=1088657#post1088657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a St did that in a game I was playing in I would probably stop attending their game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why? Do you not trust your storytellers? I only game with personal friends, and I am usually the one to introduce them to settings they know nothing about. And often for several of my games people just make mortal characters and become something else in play.<br /> <br /> But sounds kind of obnoxious to leave over something like revealing you are Kinain. All Kinain means is you are related to Changelings, it doesn't have to mean anything else, especially without other merits. Fianna are stated to have a lot of Kinain Werewolves and Kinfolk. And anything supernatural you gain wouldn't really be more significant then what you get with Gifts.<br /> <br /> You'd need to really not trust your ST, or REALLY need to have ABSOLUTE control of your Characters Family tree to just flip the table and leave over this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T02:31:07-07:00","id":1088669,"title":"","content":"Well personally I think the idea is dumb and I don't like to mix my splats. Now if the story teller was up front or at least vague about something along those lines while the group was making pc's and discussing plot I really wouldn't have a problem.<br /> <br /> Just going &quot;surprise Kinain!&quot; After games already been going for a few sessions makes me feel as a player you would rather run a changeling game (especially the book just came out) and don't have the stones to just say it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:01:11-07:00","id":1088672,"title":"","content":"Yeah these, players don't know what Changeling is, and don't know what Werewolf is. They said any game is fine, and the wild west sound neat.<br /> <br /> So should we never ever do anything from another splat? Should I have no Wraiths, and ignore the book about Ghost towns in the Wild West? Should I forbid the Fianna tribe because of the Faery connections, one of the big reasons why I am doing this because the Fianna are half the Pack?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:11:18-07:00","id":1088673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1085411-eldagusto-s-wyld-west-game?p=1088672#post1088672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So should we never ever do anything from another splat? Should I have no Wraiths, and ignore the book about Ghost towns in the Wild West? Should I forbid the Fianna tribe because of the Faery connections, one of the big reasons why I am doing this because the Fianna are half the Pack?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIts called a personal opinion guy, do what you want. You asked for an opinion on your idea, I gave one with my reasons why. No need to get all dramatic about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-06T03:16:31-07:00","id":1088675,"title":"","content":"Chill broham if you don't want me to reply to you I won't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T04:15:03-07:00","id":1090217,"title":"","content":"Help!<br /> <br /> Just curious Rage Across Appalachia is a Werewolf Changeling Crossover book, and my current game is a Wyld West Werewolf game that will deal with Changelings, so is the book any good? Cassada if I recall was always a pretty good writer.<br /> <br /> I thought this book was compiled into one of those double books, and I bought the one I was missing Rage Across the World Vol. 2 but it was Australia and Vancouver, glad I got the Australia portion though wanted that one for a while. But wasn't it in a double book? I seem to recall Valkenburg and I think Monkeywrench were another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}